`--tier global` creates `{home_dir}/_specs/` with the global README naming the resolved namespace,
and needs no attached project.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  specs:
    tiers:
      global:
        namespace: owner
-- cmd --
booping specs init --tier global
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
created dir {HOME}/Claude
created dir {HOME}/Claude/_specs
created file {HOME}/Claude/_specs/README.md
{HOME}/Claude/_specs
-- stderr --
-- expected/home/Claude/_specs/README.md --
# _specs/ — global tier (namespace `owner`)

One person's values and rules for every project, in booping's specs format — the guide is `src/specs/README.md` in the booping plugin. Referenced from a project as `owner:rule/NNNN`. Check with `booping specs check --tier global`.
